; Wrist flick in and back: flick_out.fsm on -Y, i.e. the face turns towards the
; user and back, fast, ending face up.
;
; Watch axes (Pebble): X to 3 o'clock, along the forearm; Y to 12 o'clock;
; Z out of the face, about -1 g face up. A flick rotates the wrist around X,
; moving gravity between Z and Y: turning the face away raises Y, on either
; wrist.
;
; Starting point, to tune on recordings: thresholds in g, timers in ms. The
; hysteresis is added to thresholds in "greater than" conditions and subtracted
; in "less than" ones, so the levels in the comments are effective values.
frame watch
odr 26
thresh 1 0.1        ; flick axis: neutral <= 0.0, turning > 0.2
thresh 2 0.4        ; flick axis: peak > 0.5, held and back at 0.3
thresh 3 -0.3       ; Z: face up <= -0.4
hyst 0.1
mask A -Y
mask B +Z
timer TI1 40ms      ; minimum time held turned away (rejects bumps)
timer TI3 190ms     ; neutral -> peak
timer TI4 310ms     ; peak -> back, then back -> face up
code:
  SELMA
  SELTHR1
  NOP|LNTH1         ; at or below neutral
  NOP|GNTH1         ; turning away
  TI3|GNTH2         ; ... fast enough to reach the peak
  LNTH2|TI1         ; ... and held long enough not to be a bump
  TI4|LNTH2         ; back, fast
  SELMB
  SELTHR3
  TI4|LNTH1         ; face up
  CONTREL
